--- !u!114 &1004194158
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1004194153}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: bb69fba869b9bc9498207d202d19fdc2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  questions:
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What year was Proclamation 1081 signed?'
    choiceA: A) 1969
    choiceB: 'B) 1970  '
    choiceC: C) 1972
    choiceD: D) 1975
    correctChoice: 2
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: "September 21, 1972. Marcos chose the number 21 deliberately
      \u2014 he considered it his lucky number."
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f535d54755fc80949b17029cd013c719, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What did Bagong Lipunan mean?'
    choiceA: 'A) New Government  '
    choiceB: 'B) New Society '
    choiceC: 'C) New Army '
    choiceD: D) New Nation
    correctChoice: 1
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: "Bagong Lipunan was the propaganda framework of the Marcos
      dictatorship \u2014 used to sell authoritarian rule as modernisation."
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8041b0fea58e0704ea11e22414d06ec5, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What happened to the writ of habeas corpus under Martial Law?'
    choiceA: 'A) Strengthened '
    choiceB: 'B) Moved to military courts '
    choiceC: C) Suspended
    choiceD: D) Unchanged
    correctChoice: 2
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: Suspending habeas corpus meant anyone could be imprisoned indefinitely
      without charges or trial. It remained suspended for nine years.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 61033e4bbf0b63c4588c95dd81573711, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What was COMELEC?'
    choiceA: A) A media regulatory body
    choiceB: 'B) The Commission on Elections '
    choiceC: 'C) A military intelligence unit   '
    choiceD: D) A Marcos political party
    correctChoice: 1
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: ' COMELEC administered Philippine elections. During the Marcos
      era, it certified fraudulent results.

'
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fe0d574f4bfce1a4c97615733ffb81bb, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What is crony capitalism?'
    choiceA: A) Building infrastructure with government funds
    choiceB: 'B) Giving monopolies and contracts to political allies '
    choiceC: C) Nationalising private industries
    choiceD: ' D) Foreign investment in local business '
    correctChoice: 1
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: Marcos gave business monopolies to allies like Roberto Benedicto
      (sugar) and Eduardo Cojuangco (coconut). This transferred national wealth to
      a small circle.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e7324d4413aedd1448c74fcc158a6554, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What was NAMFREL?'
    choiceA: 'A) A government media body '
    choiceB: ' B) A military intelligence unit'
    choiceC: 'C) The National Citizens'' Movement for Free Elections '
    choiceD: D) Marcos's political party
    correctChoice: 2
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: NAMFREL deployed 500,000+ volunteers to monitor the 1986 election.
      Their parallel count differed dramatically from the official COMELEC tally.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4427ea5eee69cdb408a4ac7c83b69de9, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' Approximately how many people were imprisoned during Martial
      Law?'
    choiceA: 'A) 700  '
    choiceB: 'B) 7,000 '
    choiceC: C) 70,000
    choiceD: D) 700,000
    correctChoice: 2
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: ' Human rights commissions document 70,000 imprisoned, 34,000
      tortured, and 3,257 killed.'
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bdea9819c519f914bba728dba4bf3775, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' Who was Benigno Aquino Jr.?'
    choiceA: 'A) A general who led EDSA '
    choiceB: 'B) An opposition senator later assassinated at Manila airport '
    choiceC: ' C) The first post-Marcos president '
    choiceD: D) A journalist who covered Martial Law
    correctChoice: 1
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: Aquino was shot on August 21, 1983 upon returning from U.S.
      exile. His death galvanised opposition to Marcos.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 50e8833002b96f442b0e12da8fa46d8b, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' What did COMELEC computer operators do during the 1986 Snap Election?'
    choiceA: A) Announced Marcos's victory
    choiceB: 'B) Refused to operate and walked out, citing falsified tallies   '
    choiceC: C) Certified the NAMFREL count
    choiceD: 'D) Went on strike over pay '
    correctChoice: 1
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: The walkout was broadcast nationally. It is one of the most
      documented moments of the 1986 election and a catalyst for the events that
      followed.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a493e378bc703df428c01a4008d02263, type: 3}
  - type: 0
    questionText: ' Who was the opposition candidate in the 1986 Snap Election?'
    choiceA: 'A) Salvador Laurel '
    choiceB: B) Fidel Ramos
    choiceC: 'C) Corazon Aquino '
    choiceD: 'D) Juan Ponce Enrile '
    correctChoice: 2
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: Cory Aquino, widow of Benigno Aquino Jr., ran as the unified
      opposition candidate. Salvador Laurel was her vice-presidential running mate.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5e2fba3c0a8513341a62da094b3497ea, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: ' Benigno Aquino Jr. was shot at Manila International Airport in
      1983.'
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 1
    wrongExplanation: TRUE. August 21, 1983.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b3cc97a92bdd9134ea6ae2c0987443e7, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 009cb4a2bc7275441be5e486d3bef66e, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: The EDSA People Power Revolution lasted three weeks.
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: "ANSWER: FALSE. Four days \u2014 February 22\u201325, 1986."
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a0645b25ce7f21e4ab5c93b0f8fd5601, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: ' Cardinal Jaime Sin called on civilians to go to EDSA over the
      radio.'
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 1
    wrongExplanation: TRUE. His Radio Veritas broadcast on February 22 is credited
      as a key catalyst.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b3cc97a92bdd9134ea6ae2c0987443e7, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 954fad0ebc3cf034cbac0cb145e76e19, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: Marcos was re-elected in a legitimate election in 1986.
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: FALSE. The 1986 election was documented as fraudulent. The
      COMELEC computer operators walked out. International observers reported irregularities.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fa945f3d75b557b46a5ecb52c0d2c521, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: ' The U.S. government gave Marcos asylum in Hawaii.'
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 1
    wrongExplanation: TRUE. Marcos was airlifted by U.S. military helicopter and
      eventually settled in Hawaii, where he died in 1989.
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b3cc97a92bdd9134ea6ae2c0987443e7, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 51ba5232e3ab9684291841a01eb58107, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: ' The Agrava Commission found that the government was involved
      in the Aquino assassination.'
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 1
    wrongExplanation: 'ANSWER: TRUE. The Commission concluded in 1984 that military
      officers were directly responsible.'
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b3cc97a92bdd9134ea6ae2c0987443e7, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 60497e278012a88488a433eefbf3c88e, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: The EDSA revolution involved armed combat between civilians and
      the military.
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: ' FALSE. Civilians carried no weapons. The revolution succeeded
      through numbers, solidarity, and military defection.'
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 246b8552c872263488c22fa30cb2b690, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: Ferdinand Marcos died in the Philippines.
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 0
    wrongExplanation: 'ANSWER: FALSE. Marcos died in Hawaii in 1989, in exile.'
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: cea2eb901c409fe4a85fde097d6b3f9c, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7fe04b489f287c64c9197611694f1552, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: ' Manilans held a noise barrage on the eve of the 1978 election.'
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 1
    wrongExplanation: "ANSWER: TRUE. Banging pots, honking horns, shouting from windows
      \u2014 a protest against electoral fraud and a show of support for LABAN."
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b3cc97a92bdd9134ea6ae2c0987443e7, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 74b9f0306ba7a3f4baf7051340c27231, type: 3}
  - type: 1
    questionText: ' Ramos and Enrile announced their break with Marcos on February
      22, 1986.'
    choiceA: 
    choiceB: 
    choiceC: 
    choiceD: 
    correctChoice: 0
    isTrue: 1
    wrongExplanation: 'ANSWER: TRUE. Their joint announcement at Camp Aguinaldo triggered
      the mass mobilisation that became EDSA.'
    correctSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b3cc97a92bdd9134ea6ae2c0987443e7, type: 3}
    wrongSound: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f0a3502748810e940bb8bc2e94499468, type: 3}
